+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out, Filtering the Directory by a Shown Attribute Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, and its provenance was never decided.
+
+A request on 2026-09-12 asks to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty. Read whole, NG-9 would decline that filter, so the request could not proceed on the row as written.
+
+The owner decided the row at intake (2026-09-12):
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** The directory filter stays declined. Not chosen: the owner put attribute filtering in scope.
+2. **Drop the veterinarian clause entirely.** Free-text veterinarian search opens alongside the filter. Not chosen: the owner kept free-text veterinarian search out.
+3. **Narrow the row** (chosen, per the owner's decision).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed. Free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope. Pet search and visit search remain on the row unchanged.
+
+The first capability admitted under the narrowed row is narrowing the directory to one specialty, requirement `REQ-VET-003`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The veterinarian directory and its machine-readable form can be narrowed to one specialty, reached through the address alone.
+- Free-text, partial-name, and prefix search over veterinarians still needs its own recorded owner decision.
+- Whether filtering by a shown attribute reaches the veterinarian's name stays an open question in the PRD. Only the specialty was requested, and a name filter sits close to the search the row keeps out.
+- The provenance of the row's pet and visit clauses stays part of the open Non-Goals consultation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
